//@version=6
strategy(
    "Probability Assist v2.4.6D - London Low-Volume Pullback Gate",
    overlay=true,
    max_labels_count=500,
    max_lines_count=100,
    max_boxes_count=50,
    pyramiding=0,
    process_orders_on_close=true,
    initial_capital=100000,
    currency=currency.USD,
    default_qty_type=strategy.fixed,
    default_qty_value=1
)

// =============================================================================
// PROBABILITY ASSIST v2 - RESEARCH BUILD
// One engine: LONG / SHORT / WAIT.
// Designed for a 5-minute MNQ chart with confirmed 15-minute context.
//
// v2.4.6D London low-volume Pullback surgery:
// - Reject Pullback family entries only during London when the time-adjusted
//   RVOL z-score is below -0.5.
// - RTH low-volume Pullbacks remain enabled.
// - Sweeps are completely exempt from this volume rule.
// - No probability, target, stop, WAIT, health, AMD/intermarket, scanner,
//   or alert calculations are otherwise changed.
//
// v2.4.6B short-breakout surgery:
// - SHORT family-2 BREAKOUT candidates are rejected at the final hard-candidate gate.
// - LONG breakouts remain enabled.
// - Family precedence is preserved; blocked SHORT breakouts do not become pullbacks.
// - No probability, target, stop, WAIT, health, AMD/intermarket, scanner, or alert
//   calculations are otherwise changed.
//
// v2.4.6A target-quality surgery:
// - Actual entries require a non-London structural TP1; generic ATR/R fallback TP1 is rejected.
// - WAIT setups may remain pending only when geometry can improve, and the actual fill is revalidated.
// - No probability, setup-family, stop, health, AMD/intermarket, calibration, scanner, or alert logic is otherwise changed.
//
// v2.4.5 evidence-backed quality gates:
// - Entry session filter defaults ON at 03:00-16:00 New York time; weak Asia entries are excluded.
// - Breakout Family 2 is split into exceptional momentum breaks or confirmed retest/hold entries.
// - Normal first-break entries no longer qualify without a retest unless momentum/participation is exceptional.
// - Failed Break Family 4 is quarantined: it requires a later retest/hold, strong directional flow and a post-failure structure shift.
// - Failed Break candidates require at least 4/5 evidence pillars regardless of the global 3/5 default.
// - The micro scanner mirrors the same session, breakout and failed-break quality gates.
// - Existing performance diagnostics remain active so the effect can be measured by family, direction and session.
//
// v2.4.4 diagnostics upgrade:
// - Visible performance diagnostics by setup family, direction and entry session.
// - Each family shows ALL / LONG / SHORT resolved win rates and sample counts.
// - Session win rate is tracked by the actual entry session: Asia, London, RTH, or Other.
// - Statistics use the same resolved-trade rule as the main record: TP1/TP2 = win; risk/invalidation = loss.
// - Early exits and timeouts remain censored/unresolved and do not enter diagnostic win rates.
// - Diagnostic bookkeeping is display-only and does not alter setup qualification, probability, entries, exits or alerts.
//
// v2.4.3 continuation-quality fixes:
// - Family 1 Pullback can no longer use HTF or stale structure as sufficient trend context by itself.
// - Pullbacks require a locally established EMA trend: correct stack, slope and minimum separation.
// - A real directional leg must exist before the retracement (minimum prior excursion from EMA21).
// - Fresh opposing local structure vetoes continuation pullbacks until structure flips back.
// - Pullback rejection requires meaningful directional participation/flow by default.
// - v2.4.2 true zone-touch/reclaim and opposite-impulse cooldown protections remain active.
// - Micro scanner mirrors the established-trend pullback rules.
// - Hidden family-level W/L diagnostics were added so future weak families are easier to isolate.
//
// Main v2 changes:
// - Five independent evidence pillars; trigger is mandatory, 3/5 default.
// - 15m is a modifier/veto only when strongly opposite, not a universal gate.
// - Time-of-day RVOL is preferred over generic RVOL once enough history exists.
// - ATR percentile regime changes entry behavior and probability threshold.
// - OR5 / OR15 / OR30 acceptance, sweep and failed-break behavior.
// - Faster setup coverage without re-introducing a separate scalp engine.
// - TP1 is nearest credible objective with R and ATR sanity checks.
// - TP2 is the next credible objective or bounded ATR fallback.
// - No TP2 requirement is allowed to block a valid TP1 trade.
// - Trade Health uses five independent post-entry components.
// - EXIT NOW requires multiple failure flags, not one indicator flip.
// - Displayed probability is an empirical-Bayes blend by setup family/regime.
// - Entry Quality Gate separates correct direction from bad chase/exhaustion entries.
// - Strong signals can WAIT PULLBACK when recent impulse, nearby obstacles, or exhaustion make the current price unattractive.
// - First 1-2 bars after entry have a multi-factor immediate-failure EXIT check.
// - AMD + MES/M2K intermarket context is bounded trade evidence: it can confirm reversal families and adjust directional probability.
// - Cross-market evidence cannot create a standalone setup; the original four setup families remain mandatory.
// - Alerts remain intentionally compact and unchanged.
// - WAIT PULLBACK fills revalidate current evidence/probability and never display a stale setup probability.
// - SMT comparison uses a confirmed-bar synchronization window instead of requiring same-bar sweeps.
// - Broad aligned sweeps stay neutral until MNQ confirms distribution away from the sweep.
// - Micro-only scanner: MNQ / MES / M2K / MYM / MGC / MCL.
// - Scanner runs lightweight versions of the same four setup families on every market.
// - WATCHING / PROMISING / TRADE READY states are ranked by normalized setup quality.
// - External TRADE READY alerts only fire when another micro is materially better than MNQ.
// - MGC/MCL are independent opportunity scans; they never confirm or veto MNQ.
//
// NOTE: lower-TF buy/sell volume is an intrabar-direction estimate, not native
// CME aggressor-side order-book data. A separate footprint edition can use
// TradingView request.footprint() on Premium/Ultimate plans.
// =============================================================================

// =============================================================================
// INPUTS
// =============================================================================

groupCore = "Core"
confirmOnClose = input.bool(true, "Confirm Entries On Bar Close", group=groupCore)
baseMinProbability = input.float(72.0, "Base Minimum Probability", minval=60.0, maxval=90.0, step=1.0, group=groupCore)
minProbabilityEdge = input.float(4.0, "Minimum Long/Short Probability Edge", minval=0.0, maxval=20.0, step=1.0, group=groupCore)
minPillars = input.int(3, "Minimum Independent Evidence Pillars", minval=3, maxval=5, group=groupCore)
useSessionFilter = input.bool(true, "Restrict Entries To Trading Session", group=groupCore)
tradeSession = input.session("0300-1600", "Trading Session", group=groupCore)
maxTradeBars = input.int(72, "Maximum Active Trade Bars", minval=10, maxval=250, group=groupCore)

groupTrend = "Trend / Structure"
emaFastLength = input.int(9, "Fast EMA", minval=2, group=groupTrend)
emaMidLength = input.int(21, "Mid EMA", minval=3, group=groupTrend)
emaSlowLength = input.int(50, "Slow EMA", minval=5, group=groupTrend)
